WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.406 --> 00:00:05.096
Unit four. Understanding AI Chatbots!

2
00:00:06.007 --> 00:00:11.669
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:11.719 --> 00:00:15.526
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:15.576 --> 00:00:19.888
Today we learn about Understanding AI Chatbots. Let's go!

5
00:00:20.573 --> 00:00:24.540
Chatbot. Say it with me. Chatbot!

6
00:00:28.038 --> 00:00:31.660
Prompt. Say it with me. Prompt!

7
00:00:35.226 --> 00:00:39.692
Response. Say it with me. Response!

8
00:00:43.127 --> 00:00:47.480
Training data. Say it with me. Training data!

9
00:00:51.036 --> 00:00:55.691
Accuracy. Say it with me. Accuracy!

10
00:00:59.199 --> 00:01:03.215
Mistake. Say it with me. Mistake!

11
00:01:06.716 --> 00:01:11.116
Human review. Say it with me. Human review!

12
00:01:14.551 --> 00:01:19.734
Trustworthy source. Say it with me. Trustworthy source!

13
00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:37.185
A chatbot responds to my prompt using patterns it learned from training data. Even with good accuracy, a chatbot can still make a mistake. That is why human review and checking a trustworthy source both matter.

14
00:01:37.235 --> 00:01:40.334
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:41.061 --> 00:01:46.528
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:46.578 --> 00:01:47.770
Response!

17
00:01:49.061 --> 00:01:54.708
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:54.758 --> 00:01:56.222
Human review!

19
00:01:57.203 --> 00:02:06.244
Did you know? AI chatbots don't actually 'understand' like humans do - they predict likely words based on patterns in their training data!

20
00:02:06.294 --> 00:02:08.575
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:20.260
Think and answer. Why shouldn't you always trust everything an AI chatbot says?

22
00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:21.625
Great answer!

23
00:02:22.474 --> 00:02:28.022
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:28.072 --> 00:02:31.110
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

